{"evt":"note_created","id":"note-mqaslontp50","workspace":"/Users/imyu/Desktop/zonoid","title":"Neural gate data plan: cost aware utility label, data volumes, three stage pipeline","summary":"Extends [[note-mqasdxx0tnt]] (2026-06-12). (1) Label is cost-aware UTILITY not binary solve: outcome_delta minus lambda*cost_delta — v2/v3 bench proved work parity with consult cost (1.63x fat, 1.03x lean), so binary labels over-credit injection. Live journal logs tokens+retries as cost proxies; paired ON/OFF bench arms (output_tokens) supply true cost counterfactual and calibrate lambda. (2) Data volume: ~30-50 true positives for decision boundary, ~200-500 total decisions for calibrated confidence (handoff routes on confidence); stay on 5 engineered features, raw embeddings need 10-100x more. (3) Internal continuous data is off-policy logged-bandit, NOT dirty: labels are gate-independent facts, journal raw features so threshold changes don't invalidate rows. Real risks: selection bias in abstain region (mitigate via FN post-mortem matcher + epsilon exploration) and embedding version drift (version-stamp journal rows with embed model). (4) Held-out bench = eval/calibration set ONLY, never training data (oracle-contamination lesson). (5) User repos: NEVER retrain from scratch (empty KB = abstain-only = no positives for weeks; foreign-repo onboarding was coverage-bottlenecked at 13%). Ship global model as prior, Platt-recalibrate output on first ~20-30 local outcomes, fine-tune only at volume, rule gate stays as floor.","created_by":"main","valid_from":"2026-06-12T10:37:33.593Z","vec":[-0.04498879611492157,-0.05103336274623871,0.017652135342359543,0.021921342238783836,-0.010287728160619736,-0.015284266322851181,-0.019722208380699158,0.016215989366173744,-0.00946249719709158,-0.05910007655620575,-0.03215524181723595,-0.026932716369628906,-0.031766626983881,-0.07063280791044235,-0.0485893115401268,0.01814226806163788,0.01803123578429222,-0.002871636999770999,-0.08152192085981369,-